---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy | Kvisl" description="How Kvisl collects, uses, stores, and protects personal information.">
  <main class="container page-main narrow-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Policy</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="policy-updated">Last updated 19 September 2026</p>

    <div class="policy-copy">
      <p>This Privacy Policy explains how <span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span> handles information when you visit the website, subscribe, contact us, request a licence, donate, or otherwise interact with our services. We aim to collect only what is reasonably necessary for those purposes.</p>

      <div class="policy-contact-box">
        <strong>Privacy contact</strong>
        <a href="mailto:hello@kvisl.com">hello@kvisl.com</a>
      </div>

      <h2>1. Information you provide</h2>
      <p>We may receive information that you choose to provide, including your email address, name, organisation or publication, correspondence, republication details, donation-related communications, and other information included in a form or message.</p>
      <p>If you subscribe, we store the email address needed to send new essays and occasional editorial notes. If you request republication, we may retain the information needed to review, quote, administer, and document the licence request.</p>

      <h2>2. Technical information</h2>
      <p>When you use the site, our hosting, security, database, delivery, and infrastructure providers may process routine technical information such as IP address, browser and device type, operating system, request time, referring page, requested URL, and diagnostic or security logs.</p>
      <p>We use technical information to deliver pages, maintain reliability, troubleshoot faults, detect abuse, secure the service, and understand basic operational performance. We do not use the site to create behavioural advertising profiles.</p>

      <h2>3. Cookies and browser storage</h2>
      <p>The site may use essential cookies or local browser storage for functions such as remembering your light or dark appearance preference, maintaining security, or preserving a necessary session. We do not currently use those settings for targeted advertising.</p>

      <h2>4. How we use information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>to deliver subscriptions and requested communications;</li>
        <li>to respond to editorial, rights, privacy, correction, and general enquiries;</li>
        <li>to review and administer republication and licensing requests;</li>
        <li>to operate, secure, maintain, and improve the website;</li>
        <li>to prevent misuse, fraud, and technical abuse;</li>
        <li>to keep records where reasonably necessary for contracts, licensing, accounting, disputes, and legal obligations;</li>
        <li>to comply with applicable law and enforce our rights.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Legal and operational basis</h2>
      <p>Depending on the context and applicable law, we process information because you asked us to provide a service, because processing is necessary to administer a request or agreement, because we have a legitimate operational or security interest, because you have given consent, or because we must comply with a legal obligation.</p>

      <h2>6. Service providers</h2>
      <p>We may use third-party providers for hosting, databases, email delivery, security, analytics limited to operational purposes, and other technical functions. Those providers may process information on our behalf as necessary to provide their services.</p>
      <p>We do not sell personal information or subscriber lists to advertisers, data brokers, or unrelated third parties.</p>

      <h2>7. International processing</h2>
      <p>Our service providers may operate in more than one country. As a result, information may be processed outside the country where you live. Where required, we take reasonable steps to use service providers and contractual arrangements appropriate to that processing.</p>

      <h2>8. Retention</h2>
      <p>We keep personal information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purpose for which it was collected, including service delivery, security, record-keeping, licensing, dispute resolution, and legal or accounting obligations.</p>
      <p>When you unsubscribe, we may retain a limited suppression record so that we can honour your request not to receive future subscription messages.</p>

      <h2>9. Your choices and requests</h2>
      <p>You can unsubscribe using the link included in subscription emails. You may also contact us to ask for access, correction, deletion, restriction, or another privacy request where applicable to you.</p>
      <p>We may need to verify your identity before completing a request. Some information may need to be retained where required by law, necessary to complete a transaction, or reasonably needed for security, record-keeping, or legal claims.</p>

      <h2>10. Security</h2>
      <p>We use reasonable technical and organisational safeguards designed to protect information against unauthorised access, loss, misuse, alteration, or disclosure. No internet service can guarantee absolute security.</p>
      <p>Do not send passwords, wallet private keys, seed phrases, authentication codes, or similarly sensitive credentials to <span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span>.</p>

      <h2>11. Children</h2>
      <p><span class="notranslate" translate="no">Kvisl</span> is a general-audience publication and is not directed to children. We do not knowingly solicit personal information from children through the website.</p>

      <h2>12. Third-party links</h2>
      <p>Articles may link to external websites. Their privacy practices are governed by their own policies, not this one.</p>

      <h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy when our services, technology, or legal obligations change. The “Last updated” date will be revised when a material change is published.</p>

      <h2>14. Contact</h2>
      <p>For privacy questions or requests, email <a href="mailto:hello@kvisl.com">hello@kvisl.com</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
